    "title": "What time does Pragmata release in your time zone?",
    "text": "Published Apr 15, 2026, 2:50 PM EDT Almost time for the moon landing Image: Capcom via Polygon Pragmata's release time is coming up fast, as Capcom finally prepares to launch its oft-delayed, worth-the-wait sci-fi game. Like with Capcom's other releases this year, Pragmata's release times vary depending on which platform you choose. The PC release is a simultaneous global one, but console times are staggered. Below, we break down Pragmata's release time in your time zone for PC and console. Pragmata PC release time in your time zone Pragmata launches at 12 a.m. EDT on Friday, April 17 for Windows PC. Here's what that looks like for the rest of the world: Image: Capcom Pragmata release time in your time zone on console Capcom is staggering Pragmata's console release times. It's a \"regional rolling midnight launch,\" which in plainspeak means midnight in your time zone. Areas that use PDT are an exception, as the game will launch at 9 p.m. PDT on April 16 for those locations. If you want to play Pragmata a little earlier and don't mind creating a second user account, you can try the New Zealand trick. This is where you set your Xbox console time to New Zealand's time zone (NZDT), or purchase the game from the New Zealand store on the Nintendo Switch or PlayStation. However, you will need to make an account that resides in New Zealand, and will need to swap accounts if you want to play your other games, so it's often not worth the hassle. Can you preload Pragmata?",
